  "conclusion": "The residual curvature error is systematic, not resolution-limited: it plateaus at +21..+28 % between dx = 3 mm and 1 mm for the shipped estimator, while the same MLS divergence fed with the exact radial normal converges to +6.8 %.  The bias therefore lives in the estimated normal field, and it is carried by the saturated (c >= 0.99) inner-shell particles whose normal angle error (~2 deg) is amplified by |div n| ~ 1/dx.  A one-pass Shepard smoothing of the colour field, used for the curvature only, brings the criterion to +14.2/+10.3/+6.9 % at dx = 2/1.5/1 mm while the cut-force identity stays within 15 %; the residual delta_s normalisation deficit (int delta_s dn = 0.75) is what keeps the two errors partially cancelling in the assembled force."
